course: dictionary
lesson: 6406
title: Museum: a place for old and rare things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A museum is a building where people go to look at old, rare or interesting things. The sentence «There is a pysanka museum in Kolomyia shaped like a giant egg» shows that a museum can focus on one special kind of object, and that the building itself can be surprising.
explain: Read the words around museum to learn more. «A boy in a museum in London leaned on a glass case to see better» tells you that the objects sit behind glass, so a museum is a place to look, not to touch. The clues are glass case and to see better.
explain: The word in front of museum tells you what kind it is. «A science museum» is about science, «a natural history museum» is about nature and the past, and «a museum of art» is full of paintings. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A museum is a building where people go to look at old, rare or interesting things.
fact: There are museums of history, art, science, natural history and even toys.
fact: «Museum trip» means a visit to a museum, often with a class.
fact: «A museum piece» means something very old.
fact: Museum is a noun, and its plural is museums.
exercise: «The class went on a museum trip to see dinosaur bones.» What is a museum? | A school for dinosaurs | * A building where people look at old, rare or interesting things | A park with tall trees | A shop that sells bones
exercise: «A boy in a museum in London leaned on a glass case to see better.» Why should visitors not lean on glass cases? | * Because a precious object inside can be damaged | Because museums are always closed then | Because glass cases are for sitting on | Because leaning makes the glass look cleaner
exercise: Mia says the old vase is a museum piece. What does she mean? | * The vase is something very old | The vase is for sale in a shop | The vase is made of paper | The vase is very big
test: What is the plural of museum? | museus | museumm | * museums | museumes
test: «A science museum» is a museum about which subject? | * Science | Cooking | Music | Sport
exam: «There are museums of history, art, science, natural history and even toys.» Which kind of museum is NOT named here? | A museum of history | A museum of toys | A museum of art | * A museum of sport
